1
00:00:05,189 --> 00:00:11,860
Relative pronouns are THAT, WHICH, WHO, WHOM
& WHOSE.

2
00:00:11,860 --> 00:00:18,930
They are used to introduce more information
in a relative clause.

3
00:00:18,930 --> 00:00:23,829
Relative clauses tell us more about people
and things.

4
00:00:23,829 --> 00:00:25,779
Here is an example.

5
00:00:25,779 --> 00:00:32,629
- The penetration test which we ran two weeks
ago has produced interesting results.

6
00:00:32,629 --> 00:00:36,239
This sentence includes the relative pronoun
which.

7
00:00:36,239 --> 00:00:41,079
It provides more information about the penetration
test.

8
00:00:41,079 --> 00:00:43,760
This is what we call a relative clause.

9
00:00:43,760 --> 00:00:46,959
Let’s change the sentence a little.

10
00:00:46,959 --> 00:00:51,149
- The penetration test has produced interesting
results.

11
00:00:51,149 --> 00:00:56,519
This sentence, in its basic form, does not
include the additional information and does

12
00:00:56,519 --> 00:00:59,340
not have a relative pronoun.

13
00:00:59,340 --> 00:01:05,250
Now, here’s something called a nominal relative
clause.

14
00:01:05,250 --> 00:01:08,890
- That’s what I was talking about.

15
00:01:08,890 --> 00:01:16,910
Here we are using the pronoun what to mean
the thing which or that I was talking about.

16
00:01:16,910 --> 00:01:24,370
The thing and that have combined to form the
nominal relative pronoun what.

17
00:01:24,370 --> 00:01:33,880
For nominal relative clauses, we can use WHAT,
WHEN, WHERE, HOW, WHO & WHY.

18
00:01:33,880 --> 00:01:35,290
Here are some more examples.

19
00:01:35,290 --> 00:01:38,860
- That’s not how I heard it.

20
00:01:38,860 --> 00:01:45,430
Here somebody said something, and the way
you understand what they said is not the way

21
00:01:45,430 --> 00:01:49,729
that I understand it.

22
00:01:49,729 --> 00:01:55,240
- Building awareness in their employees is
what they should be doing.

23
00:01:55,240 --> 00:02:01,120
The thing which they should be doing is building
awareness in their employees..

24
00:02:01,120 --> 00:02:07,619
Or They should be building awareness in their
employees.

25
00:02:07,619 --> 00:02:10,410
- It was when they connected the insecure
devices.

26
00:02:10,410 --> 00:02:14,250
That’s how it happened.

27
00:02:14,250 --> 00:02:18,280
Connecting the insecure devices created problems.

28
00:02:18,280 --> 00:02:20,000
This is when the problems happened.

29
00:02:20,002 --> 00:02:24,690
It’s also how the problems happened.

30
00:02:24,690 --> 00:02:28,350
- Regular security awareness training is what
we need.

31
00:02:28,350 --> 00:02:33,849
The thing that we need is regular security
awareness.

32
00:02:33,849 --> 00:02:38,060
- That’s why I’m asking you.

33
00:02:38,060 --> 00:02:44,370
Whatever sentence I said before this one is
the reason why I am asking you.

34
00:02:44,370 --> 00:02:49,230
- That’s who I’m talking about.

35
00:02:49,230 --> 00:02:53,060
That is the person I am talking about.

36
00:02:53,060 --> 00:02:57,380
The most common nominal relative pronoun is
what.

37
00:02:57,380 --> 00:03:05,349
It’s what you will hear the most.

